1
00:00:05,713 --> 00:00:10,013
(Penny:)I just love decorating the Christmas tree,
it makes me feel like a little girl again.

2
00:00:10,218 --> 00:00:12,348
(Leonard:)We didn't have a tree
when I was growing up.

3
00:00:12,512 --> 00:00:15,262
(Penny:)-Really? Why not?
-Mm, in my family...

4
00:00:15,431 --> 00:00:19,271
(Leonard:)...holidays weren't so much celebrated,
as studied for their anthropological...

5
00:00:19,435 --> 00:00:21,855
(Leonard:)...and psychological implications
on human society.

6
00:00:22,355 --> 00:00:25,525
(Penny:)Oh, sounds festive.
Did you at least give presents?

7
00:00:25,691 --> 00:00:29,321
Hm, in a way. We presented papers.

8
00:00:30,988 --> 00:00:34,028
(Leonard:)And then broke off into focus groups
and critiqued each other.

9
00:00:35,284 --> 00:00:37,454
(Penny:)Sheldon, what about you?
Did you have a tree?

10
00:00:37,620 --> 00:00:40,040
(Sheldon:)Oh, yes.

11
00:00:40,248 --> 00:00:42,288
(Sheldon:)We had a tree, we had a manger...

12
00:00:42,458 --> 00:00:46,548
(Sheldon:)...we had an inflatable Santa Claus
with plastic reindeer on the front lawn.

13
00:00:47,130 --> 00:00:50,840
To make things more jolly, there were
so many blinking lights on the house...

14
00:00:51,008 --> 00:00:53,178
(Sheldon:)...they induced
neighborhood-wide seizures.

15
00:00:53,761 --> 00:00:56,051
I take it you don't wanna
help us trim the tree?

16
00:00:56,264 --> 00:01:02,224
(Sheldon:)I do not. But if you insist on decorating
a spider-infested fire hazard in my home...

